cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "sem-particle-analyzer: watershed segmentation and size analysis of particles in SEM images"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Hj1308/sem-particle-analyzer
url: https://github.com/Hj1308/sem-particle-analyzer
abstract: >
  A Python tool for counting and sizing particles in scanning electron
  microscopy (SEM) images. Otsu thresholding with polarity taken from the
  image frame, h-maxima seeds of the Euclidean distance transform and a
  mask-restricted watershed split touching particles; per-particle area,
  equivalent diameter, Crofton perimeter, circularity and aspect ratio are
  calibrated to nanometres. Outputs number-weighted size statistics
  (d10/d50/d90, 95 % CI of the mean, log-normal fit) and a size histogram sized
  to ACS, RSC or Elsevier column widths. Validated on synthetic images with
  known particle sizes.
authors:
